{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NgS612jXfKha2Pf21C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I resolved the merge conflicts and committed the merge as `8cd98b7`. One check still fails: `npx size-limit` reports core at 4.24 kB against its 4.2 kB limit. That overage comes from the base branch, not from this merge.\n\nThere were three conflicted files:\n\n1. **`src/htm.ts`**: I kept the base branch's version. The base now unwraps escaped prop values inside `_val`, so this branch's separate `'_raw' in v` check was no longer needed. Host attributes also keep the base's browser-style rules for `true`, `false` and `null`. That `instanceof _Escaped` check only ever sees values made by the same copy, so the brand symbol isn't needed there.\n2. **`test/ssr.ts`**: I kept both sides, so this ticket's two tests for markup from another package copy and the base's parity table test all run.\n3. **`.size-limit.js`**: After the merge the browser templater measures 4.71 kB, just over both sides' limits (4.65 and 4.7 kB). Following the ticket's rule, I raised it to 4.75 kB and added that to the brand-symbol note in ADR-007.\n\n**Test results:** `test:ssr` (105), `npm test` (367), typecheck, lint, `test:build`, `test:plugins`, `test:cli`, `test:hydration` and `test:hydration-dev` all pass. The \"scaffold must contain exactly one marker\" errors in the hydration output are printed by tests that check that error is raised; none of those tests fail. I didn't run Playwright, which isn't part of the gate.\n\n**Core size:** This branch changes only `src/htm.ts` and `src/htm.browser.ts`, so the extra 42 B was added on the base branch, probably by the read-only bound props work in `src/factory.ts`. I left the limit alone because the spec plans to lower it in the later core restructure, not raise it. That means `npm run size` and `npm run gate` stay red until the base branch deals with it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":nu